{
  "requirement": "Habeas's bundled agent instructions MUST direct agents to run Cargo doctests\nseparately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: The only clause is: \"Habeas's bundled agent instructions MUST direct agents to run Cargo doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`.\" It describes what the instructions say, which is observable output. It doesn't prescribe a library, algorithm, signature, type, field or delegation. Any wording or placement that tells agents to run that command separately satisfies it, so those choices are discretionary. No structural obligation needs implementation evidence.\n\nThe supplied roots already contain the direction, so no root is missing:\n- `agent-sops/approved-implementation.sop.md` says \"Run doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`.\"\n- `assets/skills/habeas/SKILL.md`, in the \"Testing and coverage artifacts\" section, says the same.\n- `assets/skills/habeas-evidence/SKILL.md` says \"run doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`.\"\n- `assets/skills/habeas-bootstrap-requirements/SKILL.md` says the same.\n\nJudging the adequacy of the tests that assert this text is outside this assessment.\n\nbehavioral: The requirement has one obligation: the bundled agent instructions MUST direct agents to run doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`. It has no conditions or modes. The requirement declaration names four implementing files: `assets/skills/habeas/SKILL.md`, `assets/skills/habeas-evidence/SKILL.md`, `assets/skills/habeas-bootstrap-requirements/SKILL.md` and `agent-sops/approved-implementation.sop.md`.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_default_to_process_coverage_and_keep_artifacts_disposable]` is marked `{test}` for this requirement. It covers all four files:\n- **Skills, command present.** For `habeas`, `habeas-evidence` and `habeas-bootstrap-requirements`, it asserts that the whitespace-normalised text contains `` `cargo test --doc --workspace` ``.\n- **Skills, directive wording.** In the `habeas` skill it asserts \"Run doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`\". In the other two skills it asserts \"run doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`\". These checks make the \"separately\" instruction an enforced directive, not just a mention of the command.\n- **SOP.** It reads `agent-sops/approved-implementation.sop.md` through `include_str!` and asserts that it contains \"Run doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`\".\n\nThe assertions would fail if any of the four instruction files dropped the directive or changed the command, for example to omit `--workspace` or to fold doctests into the nextest run. The expected strings match the requirement. I found no other bundled instruction file that the requirement names or that carries the directive.\n\nI found no unresolved ambiguity and no marking gap.",
